<title>BELGIUM: EU vets Deutsche Bank/Commerzbank JM Voith deal.</title>
<headline>EU vets Deutsche Bank/Commerzbank JM Voith deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it had started a routine probe into Deutsche Bank AG's and Commerzbank AG's proposed joint control of JM Voith Holding AG.</p>
<p>It said in a notice that under the proposal, the shares of mechanical engineering company JM Voith GmbH would be transferred to the holding company. It added that at an unspecified later stage shares in JM Voith Holding would be sold to the public.</p>
<p>The Commission said the operation was submitted to it for clearance on March 20 under the EU's merger rules which ban creation or strengthening of dominant positions. It has about a month to approve the deal or start a full probe.</p>
<p>-- Amelia Torres 322 2876841</p>
</text>
